# Atlas CODEOWNERS — this file is the risk-class boundary.
#
# It decides which changes need the OWNER's tap and which the independent
# reviewer can clear on its own. There is deliberately NO catch-all: ordinary
# product code requires no code-owner review, so a reviewer GO plus green tests
# lets GitHub auto-merge it with zero taps. The paths below are the GUARDED
# surfaces — schema, auth, money, infrastructure, and Atlas's own controls —
# where a mistake is expensive or irreversible. Touching any of them requires
# @OWNER review no matter what the reviewer says. Substitute @OWNER for your
# GitHub handle; keep the machine account OUT of this file (a non-owner's
# approval must never satisfy the gate).

# --- Atlas's own enforcement and governance (change this and you change the rules) ---
/.atlas/**                         @OWNER
/plugin/atlas/hooks/**             @OWNER
/.claude/**                        @OWNER
/CLAUDE.md                         @OWNER
/AGENTS.md                         @OWNER

# --- CI, deployment, and dependency surfaces ---
/.github/**                        @OWNER
/.devcontainer/**                  @OWNER
/vercel.json                       @OWNER
/railway.toml                      @OWNER
/Dockerfile                        @OWNER
/package.json                      @OWNER
/package-lock.json                 @OWNER

# --- Data and money: schema, migrations, auth, billing, tokens ---
/prisma/**                         @OWNER
/migrations/**                     @OWNER
/supabase/**                       @OWNER
**/schema.sql                      @OWNER
**/*auth*                          @OWNER
**/*billing*                       @OWNER
**/*stripe*                        @OWNER
**/*token*                         @OWNER
/tests/acceptance/**               @OWNER
